## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `Game` class holds all state; `mulberry32(seed)` assigned to `this.rng`, used in `fireEvent`, `produceResources`, `ashstorm`, `createColonist`; `endTurn()` calls systems in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: 64-tile grid, `generateMap()` derives terrain from `(seed + i*73)%1000`; `buildBuilding()` checks `b.terrain.includes(tile.terrain)`; `getAdjacencyBonus()` read inside `produceResources()` multiplies output. Score 2.

**F3 — Economy**: chains mine→forge (ore→metal), soilMaker→greenhouse (ash→soil→food); caps enforced via `Math.min(this.state.caps.X,...)` in every production branch. Score 2.

**F4 — Population**: colonist objects have `skill, fatigue, morale, job, assignedBuilding`; `avgSkill`/`fatigueModifier` read directly in `produceResources()`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs**: `consumeResources()` deducts food/water per colonist, shortage cuts `c.morale`; `updateMorale()` recovers morale via `restBonus`/`medicineBonus`; BUT morale is never read anywhere inside `produceResources()`, so morale never changes output. Score 1.

**F6 — Research**: exactly 8 nodes, `available` flag gates purchase, costs deducted in `research()`; most unlocks apply real effects (unlock buildings, `construction`/`shielding` reduce storm dmg, `medicine` boosts morale) but `efficiency` (+20% production) and `hydroponics` (+30% water) are never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F7 — Events**: 10 entries in `EVENTS`; weighted selection via `totalWeight`/`r -= e.weight`; 4 events (`morale_crisis`, `merchant`, `sickness`, `pests`) have differentiated choice effects; cooldown via `firedEvents[id] = turn` checked against `turn-10`. Score 2.

**F8 — Trade**: `caravanPrices` set once in `initPrices()` and never updated; `globalDemand` written but never read anywhere; buy/sell both function via `trade()`; caravan has no inventory cap. Score 1.

**F9 — Hazard**: `ashstorm()` fires every 12 turns, severity grows with `turn/12`, reduced by `construction`/`shielding` research; but `b.health` is never read in `produceResources()` (no output loss) and no repair function exists anywhere. Score 1.

**F10 — Save/load**: `serialize()` outputs JSON to readonly textarea; `deserialize()` wraps `JSON.parse` in try/catch and `doLoad()` shows error text, but only catches syntax errors, not malformed/missing-field payloads. Score 1.

**F11 — End conditions**: win (`turn>=60 && pop>=12 && food/water>=100`) and lose (`colonists.length===0`) both checked in `endTurn()`; summary shown via `renderMap()`'s WIN/GAME OVER block, but no aggregate score value is computed anywhere. Score 1.

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab()` wired to `.tab` click listeners; log lines show `T${e.turn}`; tile/building tooltips via `.tooltip`; keyboard shortcuts (`Space`, `1`-`6`) in `keydown` listener; `@media (max-width:600px)` layout rules. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 14 real invariant assertions (caps, ranges, prereqs, hash round-trip); `runBench()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints `hash()`. Score 2.

**G1**: research unlocks set `BUILDINGS[bld].unlocked=true`, gating `buildBuilding()`, but `produceResources()` never reads any research flag to modify a yield formula (advertised `hydroponics`/`efficiency` bonuses unused) — only special-case unlock-gating exists. Score 2.

**G2**: `consumeResources()` shortfall drops `c.morale`; but `produceResources()` never reads morale for output. Only indirect link: `updateMorale()` removes colonists at `morale===0` (30% chance), reducing future production via headcount loss — a hardcoded special case, not an output multiplier. Score 2.

**G3**: `ashstorm()` sets `b.health -= damage`; `produceResources()` never checks `b.health`, so damaged buildings produce at full rate; no `repair` function exists anywhere in the file. Score 1.

**G4**: `caravanPrices` fixed at init, never mutated by turns or stockpiles; `globalDemand` object is written once and never read. Score 0.

**G5**: `morale_crisis`/`merchant`/`sickness`/`pests` choice effects each write distinct state changes (`state.restDay`, `resources.food/scrip/parts`, `colonists[].fatigue/morale`) via `makeChoice()` calling `effect(game)`. Score 4.

